      "type": "item",
      "section": "Military, defense & geopolitics",
      "headline": "Army redesignates Futures and Concepts Command as Futures and Autonomous Systems Command, absorbing five organizations",
      "lines": [
        { "host": "A", "text": "Futures and Concepts Command becomes Futures and Autonomous Systems Command, FASCOM, led by a three-star general. The Association of the U.S. Army reports Gen. Christopher LaNeve announced it on October 13th." },
        { "host": "B", "text": "What goes into it?" },
        { "host": "A", "text": "Five organizations, including the Combat Capabilities Development Command, the Medical Research and Development Command and the 75th Innovation Command. All five corps will test equipment and tactics for autonomous missions, and LaNeve said Fort Rucker will serve as the Army's drone autonomy centre of excellence." },
        { "host": "B", "text": "So this is bigger than a drone programme." },
        { "host": "A", "text": "LaNeve said the effort goes beyond drones. Folding medical research and the innovation command into an autonomy command is a structural choice, not a procurement. The Army hasn't named who will lead it. And our two sources differ on LaNeve's title: one calls him Army Vice Chief of Staff, the other acting Army Chief of Staff." }
      ]
    },
